/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (We tested five different classifiers on the dataset. In this report, I want to compare the performance of the different classifiers. The data is not linearly separable; it has a checkerboard structure. A scatter plot of the dataset in figure 1 also shows that the points in Class 0 and Class 1 follow a "checkerboard-like" pattern. This means the classes are not linearly separable, and we cannot split them with a straight line, and this means that the complex decision boundaries are needed for classifing them accurately.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
