/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (In this plot, the entire background is filled with one color blue, meaning the model predicts all points as a single class. So, the model can not  effectively separate the data for different classes. I think this is because Logistic Regression assumes a linear relationship \(straight line\) between features and classes, and if the data distribution is complex \(like here with chessboard-like\), the algorithm has difficulty to draw a meaningful boundary and capture the complex patterns in the data. As a result, this model misclassifies many data points.)
